        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Industry context</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Guest expectations now define infrastructure requirements</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>Modern guests expect fast, reliable Wi-Fi throughout their stay, seamless entertainment options and frictionless service interactions. Behind these expectations lies a complex network of access points, VLAN segmentation, IPTV distribution and back-office systems that must all work together.</p>
          <p>Hospitality properties also face significant security obligations. Surveillance systems must be robust and retrievable, guest data must be protected, and operational networks must be segmented from guest-facing services to contain potential threats.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section reveal">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 lg:px-6">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Use cases</p>
      <h2 class="section-title mb-12">Where MEAICON makes the difference in hospitality</h2>
      <div class="reveal grid-2">
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Seamless guest Wi-Fi at scale</h3>
          <p>Large resorts and multi-property groups need wireless networks that handle thousands of concurrent devices without degradation. MEAICON designs high-density Wi-Fi with intelligent roaming, bandwidth shaping and captive portals that integrate with PMS systems for automatic room-based authentication — so guests connect once and stay connected across the entire property, from lobby to pool to conference hall.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">IPTV and in-room entertainment</h3>
          <p>Modern guests expect streaming-quality entertainment on room televisions. MEAICON deploys IPTV distribution systems with multicast optimisation, content caching at the property level and casting protocol integration — eliminating expensive set-top box upgrades while delivering live channels and on-demand streaming to every room with minimal network overhead.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal grid-2 mt-8">
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Integrated surveillance and guest safety</h3>
          <p>Hospitality properties across the MEA region must maintain robust surveillance systems that comply with local regulations. MEAICON delivers IP camera networks with centralised recording, intelligent analytics and configurable retention policies — all segregated on dedicated VLANs to protect guest privacy and meet data protection requirements.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">MEA hospitality at a glance</h3>
          <p>The GCC alone has over 180,000 hotel rooms in the development pipeline, with Saudi Arabia targeting 150 million annual visitors by 2030 under Vision 2030. Guest Wi-Fi consistently ranks among the top three factors influencing satisfaction scores, and properties with integrated technology infrastructure report up to 20% higher repeat-booking rates. Across the broader MEA region, hospitality technology spending is projected to grow at 8–10% annually through 2030, driven by mega-projects, resort expansions and digital transformation mandates.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

