      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Real-world impact</p>
      <h2 class="section-title mb-12">Sector scenarios & case studies</h2>
      <div class="reveal grid-2">
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>A regional hotel group with properties across the Gulf sought to unify guest experiences under a single connected platform. Each property had independent Wi-Fi, legacy IPTV systems and siloed staff communication tools. MEAICON deployed a centralised guest Wi-Fi network with captive portal authentication that recognised loyalty members automatically, enabling seamless roaming between properties. The deployment included high-density access points in lobbies and conference areas, ensuring consistent performance even during peak occupancy and large events.</p>
          <p>In East Africa, a coastal resort chain faced frequent guest complaints about Wi-Fi dead zones and slow entertainment streaming. MEAICON conducted a site survey and deployed a mesh wireless backbone across the resort grounds, integrating room control systems and IPTV distribution over a single converged network. Guest satisfaction scores for connectivity rose significantly within the first quarter, and staff could manage room climate, lighting and entertainment from a unified interface.</p>
          <p>A North African business hotel group needed to modernise surveillance while protecting guest privacy and segmenting operational networks. MEAICON implemented VLAN isolation between guest, operational and management networks, deployed edge-recorded IP surveillance with secure retention policies, and integrated staff workflow systems over a protected wireless backbone. The hotel group achieved compliance with international hospitality security standards while maintaining a frictionless guest experience.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Case study highlight</h3>
